otherWaterproofingSpecificationAreas.value:
1. Training pool perimeter channels and surge tank, including gratings, step recesses and return pipe sleeves. Return the membrane beneath each channel flange and around the surge tank access opening;
2. Rescue equipment wash bays and drying room floor drains, including hose taps, rack anchors and doorway junctions;
   Continue the waterproofing beneath the removable wash benches and seal the drain collars before fixing the racks;
3. Staff quarters shower rooms and bathroom service risers, including shower trays, basin wastes and access panel bases. Carry the membrane behind the wet wall lining and across the bathroom thresholds;
4. Sea water intake chamber and sampling recess, including construction joints, valve supports and cable glands. Provide compatible seals at all intake sleeves and protect the waterproofing during valve installation;
5. Boathouse cleaning trenches and silt collection sump, including cover frames, grating seats and movement joints. Join the trench membrane continuously to the sump tanking beneath the maintenance platform;
6. Training centre plant deck condensate trays and discharge channels, including equipment plinth edges and drain baskets. Turn the membrane up at the wall junctions and below the removable tray supports;
7. Staff kitchen wet preparation floors and scullery walls, including grease trap access necks and pipe penetrations. Continue the membrane below the fixed cupboards and return it above each sink splash zone;
8. Coastal viewing terrace planters and irrigation channels, including root barriers, overflow sleeves and paving interfaces;
   Seal the joints around each planter cover frame and retain access to the irrigation isolation valves;
9. Emergency generator containment kerbs and maintenance wash apron, including fuel pipe crossings and the collection pit. Provide a continuous membrane below the equipment bases and over the joint between the kerb and apron.

